<IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/icons/icon3.gif" BORDER="0" ALIGN="ABSCENTER">
<FONT SIZE="1" color="#a62a2a" face="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
posted June 27, 2001 04:11 PM &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=get_profile&u=00000001" target=_blank>
<IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/profile_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Profile for Sleethr"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com" target=_new><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/homepage.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Author's Homepage"></A> &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=private_message&u=00000001"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/priv_message.gif" BORDER='0' ALT="Send New Private Message"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=edit_post&f=4&t=000005&reply_num=000000&u=00000001"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/edit_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Edit/Delete Post"></A> &nbsp;&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/cgi/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=reply&f=4&t=000005&replyto=000000"><IMG SRC="http://www.evilpumpkinracing.com/ubb/quote_ubb6.gif" BORDER="0" ALT="Reply With Quote"></A>
</FONT>
<HR size="1" color="#5d7790">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
Pets: <P>1) Learn the pet commands, especially pet back off. Can come in handy when grouped and an extra monster starts beating on someone else.../pet back off, retarget, /pet attack. Has saved a few groupmates and myself.<P>2) Know the 4 pet types and when to use them.<BR>Solo - Earth - Root..need I say more?<BR>Grouped - That gets tricky...<BR>Earth: most groups hate the earthpet. Groups like to snare monsters because a snared about do die monster runs away and doesn't try to hit back. Rooted mobs hit back causeing more damage. However; if your group lacks a snarer, get earthpet to prevent trains.<BR>Water: Good DD, Hitpoints and fast regen. Also highly resistant to poison. Can tank for a while and survive...almost as good as the earthpet for Hitpoints. A good all around pet for just about any occassion.<BR>Air: Stun...can't tank worth a damn...but that stun is great if your fighting caster mobs in a group and just good for stopping the mob from hitting back. Can save the healers a ton of mana.<BR>Fire: Tank? Forget it..thing has worse HP then Air. Only thing it has going for it is it's innate damage shield. The shield is good though...about twice as strong as the cast one, but low hitpoints get it killed fast. It is good against mobs with low fire resistances though and mobs that have many low damage melee attacks. If you are fighting a mob that casts fire based DD's, then this pet might be good due to it being immune to fire damage. It still needs to be able to survive the melee part though. It does real good against greens though.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Damage Shields ( DS ): Mage DS is the best in the game. A general rule of thumb is if the mob while hit the DS 10+ times then it is mana efficient. If more then 10 times it can become even more helpful then nuking. Helps to only need to DS on person though. Groups with 3 tanks all taunting can be a pain. You can try and see who is taking the most damage more frequently and then DS them, but it is nice to not need to worry about wasting the mana on someone that ends up not getting hit.<P>Nukes: Good nukes...only Fire and Magic based though...most mobs can be hit by at least one of the two though. It just limits you due to the mage not getting an upgrade every spell circle. That is what the pets are for.<P>Rain spells: 90% worthless. You would think that an AoE spell would be good against multiple mobs...nope. Pet's currently steal one of the 3 possible waves of damage. Only time a pet won't is against giant sized creatures. So if you are fighting giants, they can come in handy when your between nuke spell circle increases to do some good damage. High resist rates on the waves can hurt mana-efficiency, but it is nice to get 3 waves for max damage.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Debuff: Malise, Malisement & Malosi. VERY good line to have. Helps you and your pet's magical attacks hit for max damage more often. Great spell to pull a mob with due to range and utility. Also helps your group's casters hit the mob. Setting up a social with "%t has been malised!" is not only a good pull incomming warning, but signals to your group's blasters that they can start casting with less resists.<P>Summons: <P>Arrows, throwing knifes and swords are the most sought after. If you have a person pulling with a bow, offering to summon them arrows can help. Saves them money on throw away expensive items. Also, summoned arrows/knifes can hit magical. Swords are used for 29th and 34th pets to get them to dual weld and look cool. Also good if fighting summoned things, like pets or elementals. <P>Coldstones/HeatStones: If you have a night blind human in the group...give them one. Very nice for them to be able to see for a change and not need to keep casting their vision buff ( if they have one ).<P>Dagger of Symbols ( 34th ): +5MR, +5PR & +5DR. A good way to buff those stats without worrying about being debuffed by a dispell. 1 for the range slot and 1 for Primary and you just got an extra +10MR that can't be dispelled.<P>--------------------<P>Sleethr Dragynthorn
